          name: "Is MERACH cheaper on Amazon or on its own website?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually Amazon. On 28 November 2026 Amazon was cheaper by $18 to $90 on four of the six models MERACH’s store sells. MERACH’s store was $10 cheaper on the T12 Aura and may be cheaper on the T12 Pro if its $30 code applies.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does the MERACH app need a subscription?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not to use the treadmill, which runs from its remote or console. MERACH’s app page advertises a 30-day free trial but did not state any price after it on 28 November 2026, and the W50’s Amazon listing calls it a free app. Check the app store before the trial ends.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What warranty comes with a MERACH treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "One year on the frame and parts from delivery, plus a second year if you register as a member, according to MERACH’s warranty page. The page says it covers purchases from MERACH’s store, Amazon and Walmart. Amazon’s W60 listings claim three years, which MERACH’s policy does not mention.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is a MERACH treadmill worth the money?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For walking and incline walking, often yes: a 400 lb W50 TrekPad for about $256 or a 15% incline T12 for about $340 is good value. For regular running, a Horizon T101 at about $700 has a longer deck, 10 mph and a lifetime frame and motor warranty.",
          },
        },
