        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much does a MERACH treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Amazon on 28 November 2026, MERACH walking pads cost $199.99 to $282.12 and its folding treadmills $229.99 to $552.49. MERACH’s own store charged $279.99 to $499.99 for the six models it lists, from the W50 TrekPad to the T12 Aura.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the MERACH W50 walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The W50 TrekPad was $256.49 on Amazon and $279.99 on MERACH’s store on 28 November 2026. The cheaper W50 Lite, with a 350 lb rating and 10% incline, was $199.99 on Amazon. MERACH listed the W50 TrekPad at $299.99 through October and early November.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the MERACH T12 treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Amazon on 28 November 2026 the T12 cost $229.99 with 0 to 6% incline, $339.99 with 15% auto incline, $424.99 in its 320 lb version and $509.99 as the Aura with a screen. MERACH’s store had the T12 at $399.99, the T12 Pro at $449.99 and the Aura at $499.99.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is MERACH cheaper on Amazon or on its own website?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually Amazon. On 28 November 2026 Amazon was cheaper by $18 to $90 on four of the six models MERACH’s store sells. MERACH’s store was $10 cheaper on the T12 Aura and may be cheaper on the T12 Pro if its $30 code applies.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the MERACH app need a subscription?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not to use the treadmill, which runs from its remote or console. MERACH’s app page advertises a 30-day free trial but did not state any price after it on 28 November 2026, and the W50’s Amazon listing calls it a free app. Check the app store before the trial ends.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty comes with a MERACH treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              One year on the frame and parts from delivery, plus a second year if you register as a member, according to MERACH’s warranty page. The page says it covers purchases from MERACH’s store, Amazon and Walmart. Amazon’s W60 listings claim three years, which MERACH’s policy does not mention.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a MERACH treadmill worth the money?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For walking and incline walking, often yes: a 400 lb W50 TrekPad for about $256 or a 15% incline T12 for about $340 is good value. For regular running, a Horizon T101 at about $700 has a longer deck, 10 mph and a lifetime frame and motor warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

